{
  "id": "ss.enemy.scolopend",
  "name": "Scolopend",
  "description": "What an ant nest is actually afraid of, and it was already down here before you were. It shares the Courser's rig — a ringed body laid along a curve, head lifted and forward, tail low and behind, a wave travelling head to tail — because that rig is right and a second one would not be. The fringe is raked the way legs actually sit: the forward pairs reach ahead, the rear pairs trail, and the ones amidships stand straight out. What separates the two is the sentence the Courser's own document makes a point of: it has no legs. This one is nothing but legs. A fringe down both flanks, raked back, running a metachronal wave, with two trailing cerci at the tail and a pair of forcipules leading the head — so in flat silhouette the two read as a smooth worm and a hairy one, which is the test that matters. Slimmer than the Courser at radius 40 rather than 44: the narrowest doorway in the burrow is 130px and only 46 has ever been checked against the flood fill, so the boss that has to chase you through it is drawn to fit. The body's travel axis sits 18 degrees above +x, which is the `faceOffset` the game pairs with this document. `coil` holds on its last frame and `strike` opens on exactly that frame. Gameplay radius 40.",
  "tags": ["ss-enemy", "boss"],
  "size": [120, 88],
  "meta": {"radius": 40},
